{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011ChB35wuSSa4SaaENRSDh2","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"[x] `npm run lint`, `npm run typecheck`, and `npm run test:ts` pass, and the Go build and `go test ./...` still pass.\n\nTicket 07 is finished: every checklist item is done and everything is committed. Lint and typecheck are clean, `npm run test:ts` passes all 3122 assertions, and `npm test` (which includes `go test ./...`) and `go build ./...` both exit 0.\n\n1. **Projection and approval** (`src/config/trust.ts`): builds the trust projection and decides whether a config needs approval. It matches the Go approval table case for case.\n2. **Hash v2** (`src/config/trust.ts`, `src/config/canonical.ts`): `canonicalJson` is written in-house and throws on a lone surrogate. Both frozen known-answer vectors from spec 03 §2.4 match exactly.\n3. **Trust record** (`src/trust/trust.ts`): reads and writes `trust.json` version 2, atomically with mode `0o600`. A Go-era version 1 file reads as `legacy`, and approving replaces it. A malformed file makes both `isApproved` and `approve` throw and leaves it unchanged.\n4. **`roast trust` command** (`src/cli/trust.ts`, registered in `commands.ts`): prints the summary with every value escaped to one line, asks `[y/N]`, and supports `--yes`. `promptNoDefault` was added to `src/cli/terminal.ts`.\n5. **`requireTrust`** (`src/cli/trust.ts`): built and tested on its own with injected io. It is not wired into `review` yet; the ticket leaves that to ticket 20.\n\nThings that differ from the spec or that you might trip over:\n\n- **Trust functions take a git environment.** The `src/trust` functions take a trailing `{signal, env}` rather than only a signal as the spec sketch shows, so git runs with the command's environment.\n- **Missing `version` message.** A record with no `version` reports \"unsupported version 0\", matching what Go prints.\n- **Default terminal detection** was already covered by an existing test in `test/cli/terminal.ts`; I added one more that goes through `requireTrust` with plain buffer streams.\n- **Tests that passed on their first run.** The projection-order and answer-parsing tests passed immediately because the code they cover was written in an earlier step. To check they can fail, I broke the code on purpose (removed the route sort, the escaping, the terminal check, and the answer parsing), confirmed each change failed a test, then restored it.\n- **Non-ASCII in test files.** Some write paths and eslint `--fix` turned `\\uXXXX` escapes into literal characters. I fixed them and noted the eslint case in `AGENTS.md`, along with notes on the trust modules.\n\nNotes for the next attempt are in `.redeye/notes.md`, which is not committed."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":297,"cache_read_input_tokens":167795,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":297},"output_tokens":752,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"29c699d6-6603-42f0-a998-14114bd781a8","uuid":"601531ad-c9b8-4b78-a3ef-25a10645f4e8","timestamp":"2026-11-18T20:37:46.936Z","request_id":"req_011ChB35wgoFkc9PFj84H6em"}
